Bill,

From one of the web sites I found:

The Multia requires "True Parity" RAM, similar to SUN and SGI Equipment. The RAM
required is standard 72pin SIMMs, so some types of PC memory will work, provided
that they are "True Parity" (i.e. 36bit), and 70ns or better. There are 4 SIMM
slots. The multia generally can take from 24 to 256MB of RAM. The first 2 slots
take 4 to 64MB SIMMs, but the second 2 slots take 8 to 64MB SIMMs.

I still have two sets of 4x64MB 72-pin fast page mode true parity SIMMs, one set
tin-plated, the other gold-plated.   $19.95 + maybe $3.00 for First Class Mail.
Your choice, gold or tin... Ben Myers

