Hi everybody

It's been a few years, I "learned" computer science and Unix (Digital
Tru64) at school on brand new alpha 433au computers, and since then
I've ever wanted to get one of those wonderful machines...

Now it seems too late, but I've been thinking about this for a while :
- Only a few people seem to be interested in this powerful computer
architecture
- If I remember correctly, the AXP instruction set has been made "open"
(okay, the "consortium" in charge of this architecture was only
composed by DEC)
- As far as I know, HP (who bought Compaq, who bought DEC) does not
produce those chips anymore, and they're not developing anything more
for it either (They've got their PA-RISC instead)

BUT WHY?

Could it be made possible that, one day, someone (possibly a huge
semiconductors founder) make the Alpha re-birth from it's ashes like
the Phoenix ???
Would there be a legal issue, involving patents from HP, AMD, Intel,
Samsung, or anyone who took part in the AXP Adventure?
I'm also wondering how much people should be okay to support (by giving
money) this project?

Please tell me I'm not alone...



