Dear Tom & Tohris,

I've liked the Alphas from the start, when I got my hands on a 175 mhz
workstation for GIS.  Until then, doing a topology build of a
complicated polygon cover on ArcInfo gave you time for a cup of coffee.
 After Alpha, no more coffee breaks!

I have several ALphas and use an XP1000 as my main day-to-day computer.
 It is not noticably slower than the typical PC running windows XP, is
rock-steady, and it never breaks.

I would love to hear from you, Tom, what 64-bit architecture is the
best at this time.  I've been thinking about getting a Power 5 Apple,
maybe running Linux on it, maybe sticking with OSX.  I would love to
hear an argument in favor of the elegance and efficiency of the x86-64
architecture, if one can be made.  


jn



