More info about the SCSI adapter and the DLT drive in question would be 
nice, however...  The KZQSA should probably support most Single Ended 
SCSI DLT drives up to I'd guess around the TZ88.  Most of those loader 
(TZ887) and desktop drives still had the 50-pin low-density interface 
connector.  There are newer/other SCSI adapters that are supposed to 
support Ultra, too.  There's also the possibility that you could use one 
of the DWZZA or DWZZB variants to convert to Differential if that's your 
drive's interface.  Most of the older drives should be able to negotiate 
down to SCSI-I used on the KZQSA.

DLT Technology originated at Digital with the TK50 and Quantum ended up 
purchasing that whole ball of wax from us after introduction of the 
TZ87, in 1994.

http://learning.quantum.com/demo/history.htm

has the details and timeline.

bob



